# Documentation Rules

## Responsibilities

- Maintain accurate, useful documentation for developers and stakeholders
- Keep architecture, API, and database docs in sync with code
- Write self-documenting code; comment only non-obvious logic

## Best Practices

- **README.md** — project overview, quick start, env setup
- **Architecture.md** — system design, layers, data flow
- **Database.md** — ERD, model descriptions, migration guide
- **API.md** — Server Actions catalog, Route Handlers
- **DevelopmentGuide.md** — local setup, milestones, workflows
- **Inline comments** — why, not what; business rules and edge cases
- **JSDoc** on exported functions, repositories, services
- Update docs in same PR as code changes

## Coding Standards

```typescript
/**
 * Creates an invoice from billable time entries.
 * Validates client ownership and calculates tax based on org settings.
 * @throws InsufficientPermissionError if user lacks invoices:create
 */
export async function createInvoiceFromTimeEntries(input: CreateInvoiceInput) { ... }
```

- Markdown: ATX headers, fenced code blocks with language tags
- Diagrams: Mermaid in markdown files
- Keep docs DRY — link between files, don't duplicate

## Folder Structure

```
/
├── README.md
├── Architecture.md
├── Database.md
├── API.md
├── DevelopmentGuide.md
├── FolderStructure.md
├── CodingStandards.md
├── Contributing.md
└── docs/                    # Extended docs (optional)
    └── adr/                 # Architecture Decision Records
```

## Naming Convention

| Doc | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| Architecture.md | System design |
| Database.md | Schema and ERD |
| API.md | Action/handler reference |
| ADR-NNN-title.md | Decision records |

## Performance Rules

- N/A

## Security Rules

- Never document actual secrets or credentials
- Document security model and permission matrix
- Redact example data in docs

## Examples

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD ADR -->
# ADR-001: Server Actions over REST API

## Status: Accepted
## Context: Internal CRM needs type-safe mutations...
## Decision: Use Server Actions as primary mutation layer...
## Consequences: Simpler auth, no separate API versioning...
```

## Things to Avoid

- Outdated docs left unchanged after refactor
- Over-commenting obvious code
- Duplicating Prisma schema in Database.md (reference + explain, don't copy entire schema)
- README with only default Next.js boilerplate

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] README updated if setup/commands changed
- [ ] Database.md updated if schema changed
- [ ] API.md updated if new actions/endpoints added
- [ ] JSDoc on new exported functions
- [ ] Complex business logic has explanatory comment
- [ ] Mermaid diagrams updated if architecture changed
